                    also by Dunn and Matthews. See <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg395">p. 395</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1149-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1149-f2-content">
                <p>See the map facing <ref target="#pg748">p. 748</ref> in vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>. For the origin and a description of the
                        Curzon Line, see <ref
                        target="frus1919Parisv13#pg_793"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, The Paris Peace Conference, 1919, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">xiii</hi>, pp. 793</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1919Parisv13#pg_794">794</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
